//! task: write
//! ask: Keep the low nibble of a byte and set its top bit.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §5.4
//! explain: `atque` is bitwise and, `sive` is bitwise or. Hexadecimal literals are `0x` followed by digits in either case; the prefix is always lowercase `0x` (`0X10` is EXS-E0210).

publica functio larva(a: u8) -> u8 {
    redde (a atque 0x0f) sive 0x80;
}
